    "title": "Man in stolen car on the run after crashing into two cars in Raleigh - NewsBreak",
    "text": "MEMPHIS, Tenn. — A man in a stolen car is on the run after crashing into two cars in Raleigh, according to the Shelby County Sheriff’s Office. At around 7:45 p.m., deputies were searching for a stolen vehicle in the area of Raleigh Lagrange and Hoover Drive when the driver of the stolen vehicle saw deputies. They said the driver then sped up and crashed into two vehicles. The driver of the stolen vehicle fled on foot and has not been arrested. Two adults were transported to Methodist North in non-critical condition. WREG cameras captured videos and pictures of Memphis Police and sheriff’s deputies blocking the road. WREG saw a three-vehicle car crash blocking the road towards the Avery Park Apartments, and two cars were being towed. Deputies say they are investigating the accident. This is a developing story. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WREG.com.",
